<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48207" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Thisbē</span></b> , ēs,
			f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Θίσβη.</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A little town on the coast of Bœotia</i>,
				<i>celebrated for its wild doves</i>, now <i>Kakosia</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 7,
				12, § 26</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Stat. Th. 7,
				261</span></i>; <i><span class="en">9, 768</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">This-baeus</span></b> , a, um,
				adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Thisbe</i>, <i>Thisbæan</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">columbae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					M. 11, 300</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A maiden beloved by Pyramus</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 4,
				55 sq.</span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
